1
00:00:05,171 --> 00:00:09,075
With one month until
the Hakone Ekiden, Dainichi TV's crew,

2
00:00:09,642 --> 00:00:12,379
led by chief producer Ryo Tokushige,

3
00:00:12,445 --> 00:00:14,814
works feverishly on preparations.

4
00:00:14,881 --> 00:00:18,018
But Programming Bureau Chief Kuroishi,

5
00:00:18,084 --> 00:00:20,553
obsessed with ratings, pressures them

6
00:00:20,620 --> 00:00:23,123
to turn the broadcast
into more of a variety show.

7
00:00:23,189 --> 00:00:26,793
Our job as a TV station
is to show their race as it truly is.

8
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:29,596
Exactly as it happens. That's all.

9
00:00:30,463 --> 00:00:35,135
Meanwhile, at Meisei Gakuin University,
which failed to qualify,

10
00:00:35,201 --> 00:00:39,205
Coach Moroya appoints Masato Kai,
a trading company employee, as head coach.

11
00:00:39,272 --> 00:00:44,377
You're going to Hakone, right?
With the Student United Team.

12
00:00:45,211 --> 00:00:49,249
Hayato joins the Student United Team,
made up of runners

13
00:00:49,315 --> 00:00:50,850
whose schools failed to qualify.

14
00:00:50,917 --> 00:00:51,551
‎STUDENT UNITED TEAM
‎A MAKESHIFT TEAM OF RUNNERS

15
00:00:51,618 --> 00:00:55,155
Kai also takes charge
of the Student United Team.

16
00:00:55,655 --> 00:00:58,391
My goal is a top-three finish
at the Hakone Ekiden.

17
00:00:58,458 --> 00:01:00,427
Hakone would be far better off.

18
00:01:01,027 --> 00:01:05,465
But the members clash fiercely over
if teams like that were abolished.

19
00:01:05,532 --> 00:01:08,935
The unconventional policies of Kai,
who has no coaching experience.

20
00:01:09,002 --> 00:01:11,638
Mr. Kitano says
he wants to resign as coach.

21
00:01:11,704 --> 00:01:12,906
You quit too.

22
00:01:15,642 --> 00:01:19,813
Those aiming for Hakone fight
their way back from adversity.

23
00:01:26,719 --> 00:01:29,589
For the past three years,
Dainichi TV has failed

24
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:32,225
to win the ratings triple crown.

25
00:01:32,292 --> 00:01:33,993
DAINICHI TV

26
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:36,196
But this year,

27
00:01:36,896 --> 00:01:39,766
if half our programs
beat last year's ratings…

28
00:01:39,833 --> 00:01:40,667
DAINICHI TV PROGRAMMING
BUREAU CHIEF-TAKESHI KUROISHI

29
00:01:40,733 --> 00:01:43,903
…we can take the crown back from Kanto TV.

30
00:01:44,637 --> 00:01:47,340
What matters now is
the year-end and New Year's ratings.

31
00:01:47,407 --> 00:01:48,374
DAINICHI TV MANAGING DIRECTOR
MASAOMI KASHIWAGI

32
00:01:48,441 --> 00:01:49,776
And the centerpiece of New Year's is?

33
00:01:50,543 --> 00:01:51,411
It's Hakone.

34
00:01:51,478 --> 00:01:52,312
SPORTS BUREAU CHIEF
YOSHIO KITAMURA

35
00:01:52,378 --> 00:01:53,780
As Dainichi TV's flagship program,

36
00:01:53,847 --> 00:01:57,250
if its ratings don't beat last year's,

37
00:01:58,017 --> 00:02:02,122
our chances of reclaiming
the Triple Crown remain uncertain.

38
00:02:03,056 --> 00:02:04,691
Kuroishi is right.

39
00:02:04,757 --> 00:02:07,460
The Hakone Ekiden could
determine our company's future.

40
00:02:08,828 --> 00:02:10,363
-Bureau Chief Kitamura.
-Yes.

41
00:02:12,298 --> 00:02:13,766
Are preparations going smoothly?

42
00:02:13,833 --> 00:02:14,934
Everyone in

43
00:02:15,001 --> 00:02:17,403
the Sports Department is giving
everything we have for race day.

44
00:02:18,071 --> 00:02:19,005
I see.

45
00:02:19,906 --> 00:02:21,241
I'm counting on you.

46
00:02:21,307 --> 00:02:23,610
We'll keep doing our utmost.

47
00:02:25,545 --> 00:02:29,883
He's creating a plan
to beat last year's ratings.

48
00:02:29,949 --> 00:02:33,086
I could see it in Kuroishi's eyes.

49
00:02:33,153 --> 00:02:33,987
CHIEF PRODUCER
RYO TOKUSHIGE

50
00:02:34,053 --> 00:02:35,922
Why are you so scared?

51
00:02:35,989 --> 00:02:39,025
Kuroishi's pressure is nothing new.

52
00:02:39,092 --> 00:02:42,629
True, but he's on a roll right now.

53
00:02:44,731 --> 00:02:47,267
That viewer-participation
drama, The Ending Is Up to You?

54
00:02:47,333 --> 00:02:48,401
That's the one.

55
00:02:48,468 --> 00:02:51,804
It was a drama mixed with variety
elements, with viewers taking part.

56
00:02:51,871 --> 00:02:54,107
Kuroishi got that show
approved with one word.

57
00:02:54,174 --> 00:02:55,441
The one where viewers voted

58
00:02:55,508 --> 00:02:57,510
online to choose the ending?

59
00:02:57,577 --> 00:02:58,711
Exactly. And that's not all.

60
00:02:59,445 --> 00:03:02,348
He also ran drama
and variety slots back-to-back.

61
00:03:02,415 --> 00:03:05,752
Everything Kuroishi tries seems to work.

62
00:03:05,818 --> 00:03:06,853
So what?

63
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:08,922
We should have viewers

64
00:03:08,988 --> 00:03:11,524
-vote online and predict the standings?
-Oh.

65
00:03:11,591 --> 00:03:12,592
Something like that.

66
00:03:12,659 --> 00:03:14,594
Are you serious?

67
00:03:14,661 --> 00:03:16,696
Don't be ridiculous.

68
00:03:16,763 --> 00:03:19,966
We've always said the runners are
the stars. We're not changing that.

69
00:03:20,033 --> 00:03:22,035
I know.

70
00:03:22,101 --> 00:03:23,736
Despite that,

71
00:03:24,637 --> 00:03:26,973
making a good show is the minimum.

72
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:29,475
We also have to beat last year's ratings.

73
00:03:30,743 --> 00:03:34,147
Finding a way to do
that is part of your job, right?

74
00:03:35,448 --> 00:03:36,983
That's true, but…

75
00:03:37,050 --> 00:03:38,184
Right?

76
00:03:38,251 --> 00:03:41,221
I'm talking about the presentation.
The way we show it?

77
00:03:41,287 --> 00:03:43,656
We need to make an effort

78
00:03:44,490 --> 00:03:45,491
to do something different.

79
00:03:45,558 --> 00:03:47,427
Like what?

80
00:03:47,493 --> 00:03:49,762
So… you want us to dress it up?

81
00:03:49,829 --> 00:03:52,298
Not dress it up! Be creative!

82
00:03:53,466 --> 00:03:55,602
You know the rumor, right?

83
00:03:57,670 --> 00:03:59,872
About the General Production Bureau?

84
00:03:59,939 --> 00:04:01,808
Apparently it's finally
being created next spring.

85
00:04:01,874 --> 00:04:05,778
Variety, drama, news and even

86
00:04:05,845 --> 00:04:07,747
sports will all fall under it.

87
00:04:08,581 --> 00:04:11,384
If he becomes the bureau chief,

88
00:04:12,085 --> 00:04:13,820
Hakone will be a mess.

89
00:04:14,387 --> 00:04:17,056
That's why we have to beat

90
00:04:17,123 --> 00:04:20,927
last year's numbers our way.

91
00:04:22,829 --> 00:04:24,097
Seriously?

92
00:04:24,163 --> 00:04:25,331
Yeah.

93
00:04:25,398 --> 00:04:28,835
When the General Production Bureau
launches,

94
00:04:28,901 --> 00:04:30,603
I want you to run it as the bureau chief.

95
00:04:33,139 --> 00:04:34,073
Thank you.

96
00:04:34,140 --> 00:04:37,644
This absolutely has to succeed.

97
00:04:38,678 --> 00:04:41,080
I'm planning to give you
personnel authority too.

98
00:04:41,147 --> 00:04:42,682
Do what you need to do.

99
00:04:42,749 --> 00:04:43,650
Yes.

100
00:04:45,551 --> 00:04:48,955
I'll do everything I can
to meet your expectations.

101
00:04:58,865 --> 00:05:00,733
Hey. What's with her?

102
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:01,634
BROADCAST DIRECTOR
NATSUKI MIYAMOTO

103
00:05:01,701 --> 00:05:03,936
Apparently, The Other Hakone Ekiden
moved her to tears.

104
00:05:04,003 --> 00:05:06,673
Good. I thought you made her cry.

105
00:05:07,473 --> 00:05:09,676
The water stations are amazing.

106
00:05:09,742 --> 00:05:10,643
ASSISTANT DIRECTOR
CHIKA TOYAMA

107
00:05:10,710 --> 00:05:12,011
I never knew there was so much

108
00:05:12,078 --> 00:05:14,547
drama behind handing out water.

109
00:05:14,614 --> 00:05:16,983
I didn't know you had this emotional side.

110
00:05:17,050 --> 00:05:19,619
For example, have you heard this story?

111
00:05:19,686 --> 00:05:23,222
A team member who wasn't selected
became a water station attendant.

112
00:05:23,289 --> 00:05:26,559
His parents traveled
all the way to Hakone just

113
00:05:26,626 --> 00:05:28,861
to watch him run alongside
a teammate for a few dozen meters.

114
00:05:28,928 --> 00:05:30,163
That makes you cry, right?

115
00:05:30,229 --> 00:05:31,597
Me?

116
00:05:32,198 --> 00:05:33,333
I guess.

117
00:05:33,399 --> 00:05:34,233
TWO WATER STATIONS SERVE LEGS 1 AND 6,
STAFFED BY TEAMMATES OR RUNNER ASSOCIATES

118
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:36,069
The water station helps

119
00:05:36,135 --> 00:05:38,671
the runners keep going.

120
00:05:39,405 --> 00:05:41,207
It's not just to help them hydrate.

121
00:05:41,274 --> 00:05:43,409
The words
from the water station attendants

122
00:05:43,476 --> 00:05:46,145
can also give runners strength.

123
00:05:46,212 --> 00:05:48,381
Stories like this could
really connect with viewers

124
00:05:48,448 --> 00:05:50,383
who don't know much about Hakone.

125
00:05:51,217 --> 00:05:53,319
Please feature the water stations more.

126
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:57,323
Water stations? That might not be bad.

127
00:05:58,057 --> 00:05:59,225
Please.

128
00:05:59,292 --> 00:06:00,526
Look into how we could present it.

129
00:06:01,594 --> 00:06:03,196
Me?

130
00:06:03,262 --> 00:06:04,197
I'm counting on you.

131
00:06:07,767 --> 00:06:08,868
We are too.

132
00:06:12,839 --> 00:06:14,340
I shouldn't have said that.

133
00:06:14,407 --> 00:06:16,175
I'm not helping you.

134
00:06:16,242 --> 00:06:17,377
Come on.

135
00:06:17,443 --> 00:06:20,179
Mr. Tokushige,
the art staff sent over the set proposal.

136
00:06:23,116 --> 00:06:24,917
HAKONE EKIDEN

137
00:06:24,984 --> 00:06:26,619
It's not bad,

138
00:06:26,686 --> 00:06:31,190
but it feels like it's missing
something fresh.

139
00:06:31,724 --> 00:06:34,727
I told them not to change it too much.
Was that wrong?

140
00:06:34,794 --> 00:06:37,563
Right, I know.

141
00:06:37,630 --> 00:06:39,732
But even so,

142
00:06:39,799 --> 00:06:43,636
don't you want one small new touch?

143
00:06:43,703 --> 00:06:45,238
What kind of touch?

144
00:06:45,304 --> 00:06:50,510
Something that says we
tried something new this year.

145
00:06:51,511 --> 00:06:52,478
For example?

146
00:06:53,546 --> 00:06:55,882
I mean as an example…

147
00:06:56,449 --> 00:06:59,552
-So you want some kind of gimmick?
-Not a gimmick.

148
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:01,387
Creativity.

149
00:07:03,589 --> 00:07:05,892
This may sound strange, but…

150
00:07:07,493 --> 00:07:09,295
Mr. Tokushige, are you getting cold feet?

151
00:07:10,229 --> 00:07:11,664
You got to be joking.

152
00:07:12,432 --> 00:07:13,900
Of course not.

153
00:07:15,034 --> 00:07:16,369
-Mr. Tokushige.
-Yeah?

154
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:19,806
I heard Coach Kitano resigned
as a coach of the Student United Team.

155
00:07:19,872 --> 00:07:21,707
Huh? Why?

156
00:07:22,241 --> 00:07:25,545
He says an inexperienced coach
is pushing the runners around

157
00:07:25,611 --> 00:07:28,514
with a reckless goal.
Apparently, it was in protest.

158
00:07:28,581 --> 00:07:29,882
About Coach Kai?

159
00:07:30,683 --> 00:07:33,252
I've wondered about it too.

160
00:07:33,319 --> 00:07:34,320
About what?

161
00:07:34,387 --> 00:07:36,189
About how Coach Kai was selected.

162
00:07:36,255 --> 00:07:38,191
He'd been away from track for years

163
00:07:38,257 --> 00:07:41,794
and had no coaching record.
He must have known there would be

164
00:07:41,861 --> 00:07:44,297
criticism if he took over a traditional
program like Meisei Gakuin.

165
00:07:45,531 --> 00:07:49,535
I've been wondering the same thing.
I've called Coach Moroya over and over,

166
00:07:49,602 --> 00:07:51,037
but he won't pick up.

167
00:07:52,638 --> 00:07:54,574
Maybe I'll ask Mr. Yoneyama.

168
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:55,908
Mr. Yoneyama?

169
00:07:57,009 --> 00:07:59,078
He's a devoted Meisei alumnus.

170
00:08:00,513 --> 00:08:02,448
He might know something.

171
00:08:03,015 --> 00:08:05,451
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY

172
00:08:05,518 --> 00:08:06,452
HAKONE EKIDEN STUDENT UNITED TEAM
COACH KITANO RESIGNS IN ANGER

173
00:08:07,887 --> 00:08:10,656
People are taking Coach Kitano's
article at face value.

174
00:08:10,723 --> 00:08:13,092
The criticism of Coach Kai is growing.

175
00:08:13,726 --> 00:08:15,161
This isn't fair.

176
00:08:15,695 --> 00:08:16,696
Exactly.

177
00:08:16,762 --> 00:08:18,998
HAYATO AOBA
KEITO YANO

178
00:08:20,066 --> 00:08:21,567
YUSUKE MAEJIMA

179
00:08:21,634 --> 00:08:23,536
I read Coach Kitano's article.

180
00:08:24,036 --> 00:08:27,173
Maybe Coach Kai has reached his limit.

181
00:08:27,773 --> 00:08:28,608
His limit?

182
00:08:29,175 --> 00:08:31,844
He's taking all this criticism
and can't even defend himself.

183
00:08:32,945 --> 00:08:34,313
Defend himself?

184
00:08:35,114 --> 00:08:37,116
Coach Kai

185
00:08:37,183 --> 00:08:38,618
doesn't respond to critical articles

186
00:08:38,684 --> 00:08:42,288
-or abuse on social media.
-It's not that he won't. Maybe he can't.

187
00:08:43,856 --> 00:08:48,160
Mr. Yoneyama said the alumni are
making a huge issue of it too.

188
00:08:49,595 --> 00:08:52,431
But if the Student United Team
gets results at Hakone…

189
00:08:54,233 --> 00:08:57,103
You seriously think it can finish
in the top three?

190
00:08:58,504 --> 00:09:00,640
I think the individual runners
have that potential.

191
00:09:00,706 --> 00:09:02,441
Coach Kai has done

192
00:09:02,508 --> 00:09:06,178
an excellent job
coaching the Student United Team.

193
00:09:06,245 --> 00:09:07,113
What's left is teamwork.

194
00:09:07,179 --> 00:09:10,016
That's the exact opposite
of what Coach Kitano says.

195
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:16,389
Um…

196
00:09:18,024 --> 00:09:20,493
Coach Kitano mocked Coach Kai

197
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:23,262
and then walked out on the team.

198
00:09:24,297 --> 00:09:26,299
He didn't consider
the trouble he'd cause them.

199
00:09:26,866 --> 00:09:28,401
I don't think someone like

200
00:09:28,467 --> 00:09:30,670
that is fit to be a coach.

201
00:09:30,736 --> 00:09:32,171
What?

202
00:09:32,738 --> 00:09:34,507
Even you're taking his side now?

203
00:09:34,574 --> 00:09:37,209
This isn't about sides.

204
00:09:37,276 --> 00:09:38,778
Hey, Yusuke…

205
00:09:39,445 --> 00:09:41,514
I'm not asking you to support him.

206
00:09:42,815 --> 00:09:43,683
But

207
00:09:44,317 --> 00:09:47,720
can you stop believing every one-sided
criticism and making a fuss over it?

208
00:09:50,489 --> 00:09:51,757
You're right.

209
00:09:53,259 --> 00:09:55,461
You're the captain of
the Student United Team.

210
00:09:58,397 --> 00:10:01,267
Sorry for butting in.

211
00:10:03,436 --> 00:10:04,270
No.

212
00:10:05,204 --> 00:10:06,706
Thanks for worrying about us.

213
00:10:09,609 --> 00:10:12,945
I'm worried about Meisei's future.

214
00:10:14,113 --> 00:10:16,616
Coach Kai is our head coach too.

215
00:10:16,682 --> 00:10:19,785
If the Student United Team keeps
getting him dragged online,

216
00:10:22,388 --> 00:10:23,856
how could I not be worried?

217
00:10:26,492 --> 00:10:27,827
I'll eat somewhere else.

218
00:10:31,564 --> 00:10:32,798
HAKONE EKIDEN STUDENT UNITED TEAM
COACH KITANO RESIGNS IN ANGER

219
00:10:32,865 --> 00:10:34,567
AN UNQUALIFIED, INEXPERIENCED COACH
IS LEADING THEM ASTRAY WITH RECKLESS GOALS

220
00:10:34,634 --> 00:10:37,303
Kitano really did it.

221
00:10:37,870 --> 00:10:40,573
I'm thinking of refusing
to replace him. What do you think?

222
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:43,609
Yeah, that's probably best.

223
00:10:43,676 --> 00:10:46,379
Too many cooks spoil the broth.

224
00:10:47,246 --> 00:10:49,181
More importantly, are you okay?

225
00:10:50,483 --> 00:10:53,619
I'll explain it
to the runners at camp tomorrow.

226
00:10:54,153 --> 00:10:56,555
No, Kai. I mean you.

227
00:10:57,156 --> 00:10:57,990
Huh?

228
00:10:58,057 --> 00:11:01,127
With all this uproar,
you must be hearing some cruel things.

229
00:11:04,063 --> 00:11:05,331
I'll be fine.

230
00:11:06,866 --> 00:11:10,569
So you still coach at Meisei sometimes?

231
00:11:10,636 --> 00:11:13,039
Yes, as a volunteer.

232
00:11:13,105 --> 00:11:13,939
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY ALUMNI
KUYA YONEYAMA

233
00:11:14,874 --> 00:11:20,246
Why did Coach Moroya suddenly resign?

234
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:26,519
Neither I nor
the other alumni really know.

235
00:11:27,720 --> 00:11:32,458
Normally,
a traditional program would consult

236
00:11:32,525 --> 00:11:35,828
the alumni carefully
about a coaching appointment.

237
00:11:35,895 --> 00:11:38,364
At Meisei, Coach Moroya had the authority

238
00:11:38,431 --> 00:11:39,699
to choose his successor.

239
00:11:39,765 --> 00:11:42,868
But don't you think there are too many

240
00:11:42,935 --> 00:11:47,440
unknowns about Mr. Kai as a coach?

241
00:11:49,041 --> 00:11:50,209
Yes.

242
00:11:50,743 --> 00:11:53,245
Kai was three years behind me.

243
00:11:53,779 --> 00:11:58,250
He was a wonderful runner,
but he has zero coaching experience.

244
00:11:58,784 --> 00:12:02,121
Putting someone like that
in charge is a huge gamble.

245
00:12:02,188 --> 00:12:05,858
What do the other alumni think?

246
00:12:06,992 --> 00:12:10,229
Their dissatisfaction
is close to boiling over.

247
00:12:10,996 --> 00:12:12,364
After Hakone,

248
00:12:12,431 --> 00:12:15,101
they're talking about reconsidering
the appointment at the alumni meeting.

249
00:12:16,202 --> 00:12:18,137
I see.

250
00:12:20,539 --> 00:12:24,744
Actually, there's
something else that bothers me.

251
00:12:26,979 --> 00:12:28,247
What do you mean?

252
00:12:29,281 --> 00:12:32,118
Kai used

253
00:12:32,184 --> 00:12:34,520
Tohto Chuo Bussan's
social contribution program

254
00:12:35,321 --> 00:12:38,457
to accept the coaching job for one year.

255
00:12:38,524 --> 00:12:40,960
-One year?
-Yes.

256
00:12:41,026 --> 00:12:43,929
He's only a temporary coach for one year.

257
00:12:44,830 --> 00:12:46,165
No way.

258
00:12:46,999 --> 00:12:50,669
Apparently the company encourages
employees to use that program.

259
00:12:51,303 --> 00:12:55,374
There's a rumor that using it
helps you get promoted.

260
00:12:55,441 --> 00:12:58,944
So he's doing this for a promotion?

261
00:13:04,416 --> 00:13:06,418
COACH MOROYA

262
00:13:12,491 --> 00:13:15,060
COACH MOROYA (HOME)

263
00:13:23,035 --> 00:13:24,804
Hello, Moroya residence.

264
00:13:24,870 --> 00:13:27,573
Hello. Sorry to call out of the blue.

265
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:31,076
This is Tokushige from Dainichi TV.

266
00:13:31,143 --> 00:13:35,781
Oh, Mr. Tokushige! It's been a long time.

267
00:13:35,848 --> 00:13:37,082
It really has.

268
00:13:37,149 --> 00:13:39,285
How have you been doing?

269
00:13:39,351 --> 00:13:42,521
I'm managing. And you?

270
00:13:42,588 --> 00:13:43,689
I'm well.

271
00:13:43,756 --> 00:13:46,325
Are you covering Hakone again this year?

272
00:13:46,392 --> 00:13:47,426
Yes.

273
00:13:47,493 --> 00:13:51,564
Actually, that's partly why I'm calling.
I've tried Coach Moroya's cell phone

274
00:13:51,630 --> 00:13:55,100
several times,
but I haven't been able to reach him.

275
00:13:56,068 --> 00:13:57,570
I'm sorry.

276
00:13:59,438 --> 00:14:03,943
Actually, Mr. Tokushige, my husband…

277
00:14:05,911 --> 00:14:06,779
Huh?

278
00:14:08,113 --> 00:14:09,048
STUDENT UNITED TEAM
PRACTICE DAY

279
00:14:09,114 --> 00:14:11,050
I'm sure you've all heard by now.

280
00:14:12,017 --> 00:14:14,920
Coach Kitano has left
the Student United Team.

281
00:14:16,755 --> 00:14:20,459
The reason is a disagreement
over how the team should be run.

282
00:14:20,526 --> 00:14:21,360
JO INOMATA, TAKUMI SAKIYAMA
MAKOTO AMAGI

283
00:14:21,427 --> 00:14:24,864
I'm sorry this happened at a time

284
00:14:24,930 --> 00:14:26,732
when you should be focused.

285
00:14:28,133 --> 00:14:29,902
This is entirely my responsibility.

286
00:14:32,638 --> 00:14:33,639
I'm sorry.

287
00:14:37,376 --> 00:14:38,377
Um…

288
00:14:39,445 --> 00:14:41,847
Is Kota leaving too?

289
00:14:43,148 --> 00:14:44,950
I haven't heard anything from Kota yet.

290
00:14:45,017 --> 00:14:48,020
So he hasn't said he's quitting?

291
00:14:49,054 --> 00:14:49,922
But

292
00:14:50,456 --> 00:14:53,525
his university coach, the man
he's followed all this time walked away.

293
00:14:55,761 --> 00:14:59,598
All we can do now is wait,
but Kota will probably come.

294
00:15:22,922 --> 00:15:26,558
I'm thinking of quitting
as coach of the Student United Team.

295
00:15:26,625 --> 00:15:27,493
KOTA MATSUKI

296
00:15:27,559 --> 00:15:28,427
Huh?

297
00:15:28,494 --> 00:15:29,795
Kai is the laughingstock

298
00:15:29,862 --> 00:15:31,931
of the track and field world now.

299
00:15:31,997 --> 00:15:33,232
‎COACH SEIWA INTERNATIONAL
‎STUDENT UNITED TEAM-KOICHI KITANO

300
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:35,901
You quit too.

301
00:15:36,969 --> 00:15:40,539
I'll notify the Kanto Student Federation
of my resignation tomorrow.

302
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:42,775
You withdraw too.

303
00:15:44,543 --> 00:15:45,611
Understood?

304
00:15:53,285 --> 00:15:55,454
KEITO YANO

305
00:15:59,391 --> 00:16:01,327
HOSPICE CARE

306
00:16:02,695 --> 00:16:03,762
Yes?

307
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:08,167
Excuse me.

308
00:16:08,968 --> 00:16:12,805
What?
Why did you come all the way out here?

309
00:16:12,871 --> 00:16:13,772
I'm sorry.

310
00:16:14,506 --> 00:16:16,842
You wouldn't answer your phone.

311
00:16:17,843 --> 00:16:20,446
I'm doing a digital detox.

312
00:16:21,914 --> 00:16:25,684
I'm impressed you
know such a trendy phrase.

313
00:16:26,285 --> 00:16:27,853
Of course I do.

314
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:31,991
No matter how old I get,
I've spent my life dealing with

315
00:16:32,057 --> 00:16:34,293
young college students.

316
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:37,296
I've had to learn how
to communicate with them.

317
00:16:38,630 --> 00:16:39,498
True.

318
00:16:40,265 --> 00:16:43,736
Coach Kitano quit the Student United Team?

319
00:16:44,269 --> 00:16:45,237
Yes.

320
00:16:46,138 --> 00:16:49,641
And recently,
Coach Hirakawa of Tozai University

321
00:16:50,209 --> 00:16:52,511
criticized the Student United Team.

322
00:16:52,578 --> 00:16:56,715
Coach Kai is taking a lot of abuse online.

323
00:16:56,782 --> 00:16:58,984
So that's what's happening.

324
00:17:00,285 --> 00:17:05,591
There's something I've wanted to ask you.

325
00:17:06,291 --> 00:17:09,561
Why did you name Mr. Kai your successor?

326
00:17:10,963 --> 00:17:13,732
Someone like Yoneyama

327
00:17:13,799 --> 00:17:16,301
could probably have succeeded me.

328
00:17:17,136 --> 00:17:20,806
If all I wanted was to maintain
the status quo, that would've been fine.

329
00:17:21,640 --> 00:17:22,841
But

330
00:17:23,375 --> 00:17:26,245
if I wanted to take Meisei

331
00:17:26,311 --> 00:17:29,114
to a new level,

332
00:17:29,181 --> 00:17:31,083
it had to be Masato Kai.

333
00:17:31,717 --> 00:17:33,819
I couldn't think of anyone else.

334
00:17:35,421 --> 00:17:36,855
You really trust him.

335
00:17:38,457 --> 00:17:42,094
Well, he's unproven as a coach.

336
00:17:43,028 --> 00:17:47,032
But he has imagination

337
00:17:47,099 --> 00:17:48,734
and flexibility.

338
00:17:48,801 --> 00:17:51,537
So you truly believe Coach Kai

339
00:17:51,603 --> 00:17:54,907
can build a new powerhouse.

340
00:17:55,641 --> 00:17:56,909
Is that so?

341
00:17:57,509 --> 00:17:59,545
Not just Meisei.

342
00:18:00,913 --> 00:18:02,448
The Student United Team too.

343
00:18:03,982 --> 00:18:05,951
Kai will change

344
00:18:06,819 --> 00:18:09,321
the history of Hakone.

345
00:18:13,492 --> 00:18:16,128
Kota didn't come after all.

346
00:18:16,795 --> 00:18:18,931
Maybe Coach Kitano stopped him.

347
00:18:18,997 --> 00:18:22,067
What does the coach have to do with it?

348
00:18:22,134 --> 00:18:23,836
We're the ones who run.

349
00:18:23,902 --> 00:18:26,271
-Yeah.
-Right?

350
00:18:26,338 --> 00:18:27,573
Still, I don't know.

351
00:18:28,107 --> 00:18:29,541
I feel like I'm here

352
00:18:29,608 --> 00:18:31,810
because of Coach Onuma.

353
00:18:31,877 --> 00:18:33,879
So I understand Kota a little.

354
00:18:38,150 --> 00:18:41,019
Kota was fast
at the time trial, wasn't he?

355
00:18:44,723 --> 00:18:46,658
He was amazing.

356
00:18:49,027 --> 00:18:52,397
If Kota leaves, we're in trouble.

357
00:18:54,399 --> 00:18:55,834
Then why don't you leave with him?

358
00:18:55,901 --> 00:18:57,402
You were hanging around with him.

359
00:18:59,571 --> 00:19:01,406
You're the one who was always with Kota.

360
00:19:01,473 --> 00:19:03,375
-You were!
-Um…

361
00:19:04,443 --> 00:19:05,444
Let's stop.

362
00:19:05,978 --> 00:19:06,812
Yeah.

363
00:19:07,479 --> 00:19:09,381
This is when we need to pull together.

364
00:19:10,282 --> 00:19:13,485
But this is Coach Kai's
fault in the first place.

365
00:19:13,552 --> 00:19:15,854
We know the coach isn't the bad guy.

366
00:19:16,622 --> 00:19:20,959
Actually, I once interviewed

367
00:19:21,026 --> 00:19:22,928
Mr. Kai when he was a runner.

368
00:19:22,995 --> 00:19:25,197
-I see.
-Yes.

369
00:19:27,065 --> 00:19:31,870
That interview became a kind of
a trauma for me as a TV journalist.

370
00:19:33,539 --> 00:19:34,907
A little wound

371
00:19:35,474 --> 00:19:37,109
I'd rather not remember.

372
00:19:38,610 --> 00:19:40,612
Did Kai say something to you?

373
00:19:43,415 --> 00:19:45,484
You could say that.

374
00:19:45,551 --> 00:19:46,385
20 YEARS AGO
HAKONE EKIDEN-TOTSUKA RELAY POINT

375
00:19:46,451 --> 00:19:48,520
Congratulations on the
fastest time on the second leg.

376
00:19:48,587 --> 00:19:49,421
Thank you.

377
00:19:49,488 --> 00:19:50,622
That was an incredible run.

378
00:19:50,689 --> 00:19:51,523
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY FIRST-YEAR
MASATO KAI

379
00:19:51,590 --> 00:19:53,358
How did you feel when you
crossed the goal first?

380
00:19:54,059 --> 00:19:55,127
It's "finish."

381
00:19:56,295 --> 00:19:58,730
In track and field,
we say "finish," not "goal."

382
00:20:01,633 --> 00:20:04,870
-I'd just joined the Sports Department,
-I'm sorry.

383
00:20:04,937 --> 00:20:06,872
but I hadn't done my homework.

384
00:20:06,939 --> 00:20:08,307
I mean…

385
00:20:09,208 --> 00:20:11,677
I was so embarrassed and ashamed.

386
00:20:12,411 --> 00:20:15,547
I've never been able to
watch that interview again.

387
00:20:16,848 --> 00:20:18,884
That does sound like Kai.

388
00:20:19,451 --> 00:20:21,620
He probably couldn't forgive a TV reporter

389
00:20:21,687 --> 00:20:24,790
who couldn't report on track properly.

390
00:20:24,856 --> 00:20:25,691
Yes.

391
00:20:26,558 --> 00:20:30,195
Still, getting embarrassed
by a college kid

392
00:20:30,262 --> 00:20:33,665
much younger than you must have hurt.

393
00:20:34,566 --> 00:20:35,434
Yes.

394
00:20:36,034 --> 00:20:39,004
People at the station
teased me about it for a while.

395
00:20:39,738 --> 00:20:42,641
But that bitter experience is why

396
00:20:43,475 --> 00:20:46,445
I can now demand thorough research

397
00:20:47,512 --> 00:20:52,451
from my staff.

398
00:21:04,596 --> 00:21:07,966
Hello. I'm Tokushige from Dainichi TV.

399
00:21:08,867 --> 00:21:10,369
Why are you here?

400
00:21:12,070 --> 00:21:14,273
Coach Moroya's wife told me.

401
00:21:15,140 --> 00:21:16,074
I see.

402
00:21:17,009 --> 00:21:20,078
I finally understand why Coach Moroya

403
00:21:20,712 --> 00:21:21,847
resigned so suddenly.

404
00:21:23,048 --> 00:21:24,983
I'd appreciate it if you didn't report it.

405
00:21:25,050 --> 00:21:26,385
Of course.

406
00:21:26,451 --> 00:21:29,054
I'll respect the coach's wishes

407
00:21:29,121 --> 00:21:31,590
not to upset the runners.

408
00:21:32,224 --> 00:21:33,058
Please.

409
00:21:33,859 --> 00:21:36,995
By the way, the runners seem distracted

410
00:21:37,062 --> 00:21:40,299
by something else right now.

411
00:21:40,365 --> 00:21:41,933
Will they be okay?

412
00:21:42,768 --> 00:21:44,536
Yes. Don't worry.

413
00:21:46,038 --> 00:21:49,007
This isn't an interview.

414
00:21:49,574 --> 00:21:53,545
I'd like to ask you something personally.

415
00:21:55,147 --> 00:21:56,615
Why did you

416
00:21:57,182 --> 00:22:00,218
agree to succeed Coach Moroya?

417
00:22:02,254 --> 00:22:04,389
I don't think I need to answer that.

418
00:22:08,260 --> 00:22:11,830
I respect Coach Moroya.

419
00:22:12,331 --> 00:22:16,601
I want to believe he was right

420
00:22:16,668 --> 00:22:18,537
to entrust everything to you.

421
00:22:19,504 --> 00:22:22,207
But I still can't understand

422
00:22:22,274 --> 00:22:28,480
what kind of man Masato Kai is.

423
00:22:30,115 --> 00:22:33,018
I think you'll understand
if you watch the race.

424
00:22:33,785 --> 00:22:34,619
Huh?

425
00:22:34,686 --> 00:22:39,291
The result will prove Coach Moroya
made the right choice.

426
00:22:42,761 --> 00:22:43,729
Excuse me.

427
00:22:47,699 --> 00:22:50,235
That was way too cool.

428
00:22:53,872 --> 00:22:56,007
I heard from Tokushige.

429
00:22:56,942 --> 00:23:01,480
You didn't have to come
see me when you've got so much going on.

430
00:23:05,384 --> 00:23:09,087
I came to apologize today.

431
00:23:10,288 --> 00:23:12,924
You have nothing to apologize to me for.

432
00:23:13,892 --> 00:23:17,028
Everything that happened
is due to my shortcomings.

433
00:23:20,165 --> 00:23:23,268
You still have a lot of enemies.

434
00:23:24,803 --> 00:23:27,105
The nail that sticks out
gets hammered down.

435
00:23:27,606 --> 00:23:29,808
I don't care what people say about me.

436
00:23:30,409 --> 00:23:31,243
But

437
00:23:31,943 --> 00:23:34,579
I never wanted the runners
to suffer because of it.

438
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:36,848
I feel terrible about that.

439
00:23:37,849 --> 00:23:40,185
You knew what you were getting into?

440
00:23:42,287 --> 00:23:46,458
I couldn't have accepted a responsibility
this big without being prepared.

441
00:23:49,094 --> 00:23:49,995
I see.

442
00:23:50,495 --> 00:23:51,730
Yes.

443
00:23:55,767 --> 00:23:59,471
I was talking with Tokushige earlier.

444
00:24:01,239 --> 00:24:03,975
It made me wonder again.

445
00:24:05,510 --> 00:24:09,347
Why did you accept

446
00:24:09,414 --> 00:24:13,885
my request?
He wanted to know the reason too.

447
00:24:15,353 --> 00:24:17,722
Now you're asking?

448
00:24:19,057 --> 00:24:21,760
Yeah. I'm asking now.

449
00:24:22,828 --> 00:24:24,596
There are several reasons.

450
00:24:25,230 --> 00:24:28,333
One is something you taught me.

451
00:24:31,036 --> 00:24:32,037
Me?

452
00:24:33,004 --> 00:24:33,972
Yes.

453
00:24:35,540 --> 00:24:37,209
A crucial second shot.

454
00:24:37,275 --> 00:24:40,645
Ogiso has practiced shots
from this distance over and over.

455
00:24:40,712 --> 00:24:41,913
This one's going to get close!

456
00:24:43,849 --> 00:24:44,683
What a shot!

457
00:24:44,749 --> 00:24:47,152
-Mr. Karashima sure is something else.
-Past the pin! A birdie chance!

458
00:24:47,219 --> 00:24:49,154
For better or worse,

459
00:24:49,221 --> 00:24:51,223
Dainichi Golf coverage
is synonymous with Karashima.

460
00:24:51,289 --> 00:24:52,991
He's a pain, though.

461
00:24:53,058 --> 00:24:54,392
We're in a meeting.

462
00:24:54,459 --> 00:24:56,428
Hey! You don't have to turn it off!

463
00:24:56,495 --> 00:24:58,063
We'll still do the meeting.

464
00:24:58,129 --> 00:25:00,165
Then I'll mute it.

465
00:25:00,232 --> 00:25:01,466
Good morning.

466
00:25:01,533 --> 00:25:02,901
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

467
00:25:06,371 --> 00:25:07,472
THE NEW DESIGN-MIYAMOTO

468
00:25:07,539 --> 00:25:10,275
Huh? Mr. Tokushige never came back?

469
00:25:10,342 --> 00:25:12,310
Maybe it really can't be done.

470
00:25:12,377 --> 00:25:14,946
The crowd noise is huge.

471
00:25:15,013 --> 00:25:17,082
You're here on a Sunday? That's rare.

472
00:25:17,148 --> 00:25:20,185
I was watching old footage
until late last night,

473
00:25:20,252 --> 00:25:21,987
and something
about the voices bothered me.

474
00:25:22,053 --> 00:25:23,321
-The voices?
-Yes.

475
00:25:23,388 --> 00:25:24,656
The voices at the water station.

476
00:25:25,223 --> 00:25:27,893
Those two runners have been
classmates since high school.

477
00:25:27,959 --> 00:25:30,795
Kawaguchi was running Hakone
for the first time.

478
00:25:30,862 --> 00:25:34,199
Suzuki was injured and left off the team,
so he was assigned to the water station.

479
00:25:34,266 --> 00:25:37,068
They were both seniors,
and it was their last Hakone.

480
00:25:37,135 --> 00:25:38,737
Oh, that was last year.

481
00:25:38,803 --> 00:25:39,738
Yes.

482
00:25:39,804 --> 00:25:41,873
Kawaguchi was nervous.

483
00:25:41,940 --> 00:25:45,977
Suzuki promised he'd make him laugh
while running beside him with water.

484
00:25:46,044 --> 00:25:47,979
I saw it on The Other Hakone Ekiden.

485
00:25:48,046 --> 00:25:51,950
But I couldn't hear what
Suzuki said to make him laugh.

486
00:25:52,017 --> 00:25:54,986
Getting clear audio in a crowd

487
00:25:55,053 --> 00:25:55,987
that loud is difficult.

488
00:25:56,054 --> 00:25:58,290
It feels like there should be some way.

489
00:25:58,356 --> 00:26:00,559
If there were, we'd already do it.

490
00:26:00,625 --> 00:26:02,827
I guess so…

491
00:26:03,628 --> 00:26:05,864
Oh! If he sinks this, he'll take the lead.

492
00:26:06,798 --> 00:26:09,568
Now, a birdie putt.

493
00:26:09,634 --> 00:26:10,835
OGISO

494
00:26:10,902 --> 00:26:12,203
Middle of the putt...

495
00:26:12,270 --> 00:26:14,372
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

496
00:26:15,140 --> 00:26:16,541
-That sound just now!
-Huh?

497
00:26:16,608 --> 00:26:17,976
How are they recording that?

498
00:26:18,043 --> 00:26:18,944
What?

499
00:26:19,010 --> 00:26:21,046
The sound of the ball
dropping into the cup.

500
00:26:21,112 --> 00:26:22,847
It was incredibly clear, wasn't it?

501
00:26:22,914 --> 00:26:24,716
But you can't see a microphone on screen.

502
00:26:26,017 --> 00:26:27,319
Mr. Kuwana.

503
00:26:27,385 --> 00:26:29,354
Have we ever used that golf shotgun mic

504
00:26:29,421 --> 00:26:30,789
at a Hakone water station?

505
00:26:30,855 --> 00:26:34,159
-We're in a meeting.
-Yeah…

506
00:26:35,026 --> 00:26:36,928
As far as I know, no.

507
00:26:36,995 --> 00:26:39,197
Then could one of those mics pick up

508
00:26:39,264 --> 00:26:40,765
a runner's voice during the race?

509
00:26:40,832 --> 00:26:43,501
But Hakone is different…

510
00:26:44,202 --> 00:26:46,004
With those crowds, it would be difficult.

511
00:26:46,071 --> 00:26:48,173
But the chance isn't zero.

512
00:26:50,709 --> 00:26:53,211
Maybe not zero.

513
00:26:54,179 --> 00:26:55,380
Can we test it?

514
00:26:55,447 --> 00:26:57,315
-I said we're in a meeting!
-Hey!

515
00:26:57,382 --> 00:26:58,883
Help her get the equipment.

516
00:26:58,950 --> 00:26:59,818
Yes.

517
00:27:00,485 --> 00:27:01,886
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

518
00:27:04,689 --> 00:27:06,758
Guys! Look!

519
00:27:07,392 --> 00:27:08,560
Did you see this?

520
00:27:10,028 --> 00:27:11,563
This is awful.

521
00:27:11,630 --> 00:27:12,464
DO WE EVEN NEED A STUDENT UNITED TEAM?
PROBABLY DON'T NEED THEM

522
00:27:12,530 --> 00:27:13,665
Here's another one.

523
00:27:16,434 --> 00:27:19,237
"We don't need the Student United Team."

524
00:27:19,771 --> 00:27:21,706
"Who'd be moved by rivals

525
00:27:21,773 --> 00:27:24,576
from different schools
passing a sash to each other?"

526
00:27:24,643 --> 00:27:25,844
That's what it says.

527
00:27:25,910 --> 00:27:26,978
That's messed up.

528
00:27:27,045 --> 00:27:28,980
"People still see the Student United Team

529
00:27:29,047 --> 00:27:31,216
as runners
pulling in different directions…"

530
00:27:31,282 --> 00:27:33,351
The criticism on social
media is really catching fire.

531
00:27:33,418 --> 00:27:34,819
-Huh?
-Who said that?

532
00:27:34,886 --> 00:27:37,222
-That pisses me off!
-That's awful, isn't it?

533
00:27:37,288 --> 00:27:38,556
I see.

534
00:27:39,691 --> 00:27:40,825
Yes.

535
00:27:40,892 --> 00:27:44,963
We were finally starting to come together.

536
00:27:45,030 --> 00:27:47,298
But everyone thinks differently,

537
00:27:47,832 --> 00:27:49,567
and we're losing focus.

538
00:27:50,669 --> 00:27:54,639
As ฉaptain, what should I say to them?

539
00:27:57,642 --> 00:27:58,543
Hayato.

540
00:27:59,244 --> 00:28:00,345
Yes?

541
00:28:01,312 --> 00:28:03,715
Don't forget the most important thing.

542
00:28:06,117 --> 00:28:08,853
Our goal of finishing in the top three?

543
00:28:10,689 --> 00:28:11,956
Then…

544
00:28:15,727 --> 00:28:18,396
You and Mr. Kai joined the company
at the same time, right?

545
00:28:18,963 --> 00:28:19,898
Yes.

546
00:28:20,532 --> 00:28:24,836
Mr. Kai still technically has a position
at the company, doesn't he?

547
00:28:24,903 --> 00:28:25,904
KAI'S COLLEAGUE AT TOHTO CHUO BUSSAN
REIJI WAKUDA

548
00:28:25,970 --> 00:28:29,307
He's using the one-year
social contribution program.

549
00:28:30,709 --> 00:28:34,612
So he'll coach for one year

550
00:28:34,679 --> 00:28:37,982
and then return to the company?

551
00:28:39,250 --> 00:28:40,085
No.

552
00:28:41,553 --> 00:28:43,254
Knowing Kai,

553
00:28:44,656 --> 00:28:46,658
I think he accepted the coaching job

554
00:28:47,192 --> 00:28:48,827
intending never to return.

555
00:28:49,461 --> 00:28:52,630
Then why use the program

556
00:28:52,697 --> 00:28:54,399
instead of resigning?

557
00:28:55,934 --> 00:28:57,669
He never told me,

558
00:28:59,237 --> 00:29:03,775
but I think it was
so he wouldn't receive coaching pay

559
00:29:03,842 --> 00:29:05,744
from the university for one year.

560
00:29:08,046 --> 00:29:11,883
You mean Mr. Kai wanted his coaching pay

561
00:29:12,417 --> 00:29:14,419
to go to the team instead?

562
00:29:15,954 --> 00:29:18,957
That's probably what he intended.

563
00:29:19,724 --> 00:29:20,725
But

564
00:29:20,792 --> 00:29:24,262
what about his work at the company?

565
00:29:25,063 --> 00:29:28,833
I heard he had a career

566
00:29:28,900 --> 00:29:30,135
that took him around the world.

567
00:29:32,904 --> 00:29:33,772
Yes.

568
00:29:35,807 --> 00:29:36,641
He did.

569
00:29:38,109 --> 00:29:39,177
He did?

570
00:29:42,247 --> 00:29:45,984
Back then, Kai poured even more passion

571
00:29:46,050 --> 00:29:48,286
into his work than anyone else.

572
00:29:48,353 --> 00:29:51,723
What kind of work did he do?

573
00:29:53,291 --> 00:29:54,893
He was in the steel division's

574
00:29:54,959 --> 00:29:57,362
prestigious overseas department.

575
00:29:57,428 --> 00:29:59,964
He led several successful M&amp;A deals

576
00:30:00,031 --> 00:30:01,866
with an eye to future growth.

577
00:30:03,535 --> 00:30:05,870
His direct supervisor at the time

578
00:30:05,937 --> 00:30:07,372
was a department head named Harada.

579
00:30:07,438 --> 00:30:09,207
TOHTO CHUO BUSSAN

580
00:30:10,842 --> 00:30:12,677
You did it, Kai!

581
00:30:12,744 --> 00:30:15,580
I'm lucky to have
such a dependable subordinate.

582
00:30:16,447 --> 00:30:17,682
Thank you.

583
00:30:21,452 --> 00:30:24,589
Harada favored Kai,

584
00:30:25,256 --> 00:30:27,158
and Kai respected him.

585
00:30:28,526 --> 00:30:29,661
Three years ago,

586
00:30:30,295 --> 00:30:34,232
Kai was put in charge
of acquiring a mine in Brazil.

587
00:30:36,534 --> 00:30:39,170
At first, Kai refused.

588
00:30:39,237 --> 00:30:42,974
He said the long-term risk was too high.

589
00:30:44,008 --> 00:30:45,076
But…

590
00:30:45,944 --> 00:30:48,947
This is the president's project.

591
00:30:49,681 --> 00:30:50,548
However,

592
00:30:51,316 --> 00:30:54,252
there are serious concerns

593
00:30:54,319 --> 00:30:56,154
about this company's environmental record.

594
00:30:57,121 --> 00:30:59,190
Signing this deal is too risky.

595
00:30:59,257 --> 00:31:03,127
The president already gave
his verbal approval.

596
00:31:06,231 --> 00:31:07,932
-Even so--
-Kai.

597
00:31:08,967 --> 00:31:12,637
That uncompromising integrity of yours

598
00:31:13,204 --> 00:31:16,507
is both a strength and a weakness.

599
00:31:18,643 --> 00:31:21,446
Sometimes you need to be flexible.

600
00:31:23,081 --> 00:31:25,183
-But--
-Don't worry.

601
00:31:25,750 --> 00:31:29,554
If anything happens,
I'll take responsibility.

602
00:31:31,990 --> 00:31:37,629
I think Kai wanted to trust Harada.

603
00:31:39,631 --> 00:31:43,668
But later, environmental problems
at the acquired company came to light.

604
00:31:43,735 --> 00:31:46,137
-Hey, this is bad.
-Then they discovered

605
00:31:46,204 --> 00:31:48,106
a company-wide cover-up.

606
00:31:48,172 --> 00:31:50,675
-They went bankrupt.
-The company

607
00:31:50,742 --> 00:31:52,911
was left with enormous losses.

608
00:31:52,977 --> 00:31:54,946
-We're going to get busy.
-Yeah.

609
00:31:55,546 --> 00:31:56,514
Kai.

610
00:31:57,081 --> 00:32:00,418
I need you to wrap
this matter up properly.

611
00:32:01,119 --> 00:32:02,020
Yes.

612
00:32:02,086 --> 00:32:04,722
That's your duty as project leader.

613
00:32:06,925 --> 00:32:09,594
When this project started two years ago,

614
00:32:10,328 --> 00:32:12,430
I warned you, didn't I?

615
00:32:13,097 --> 00:32:16,000
I understand you want
to avoid responsibility, but…

616
00:32:19,170 --> 00:32:20,605
Wait.

617
00:32:21,606 --> 00:32:26,144
You told me that if anything
happened, you would take responsibility.

618
00:32:27,679 --> 00:32:29,881
I don't remember saying that.

619
00:32:35,787 --> 00:32:40,058
Kai received a formal reprimand
in the president's name.

620
00:32:42,427 --> 00:32:46,731
He was transferred to a department
considered a dead end inside the company.

621
00:32:48,199 --> 00:32:49,567
After that,

622
00:32:51,769 --> 00:32:53,938
he clearly lost all his motivation.

623
00:32:56,808 --> 00:33:00,945
I never expected Mr. Harada
to take responsibility.

624
00:33:02,447 --> 00:33:04,415
I knew he'd protect himself.

625
00:33:06,651 --> 00:33:08,286
At first, I believed in him.

626
00:33:09,053 --> 00:33:10,188
In my boss,

627
00:33:11,155 --> 00:33:12,890
and in the company's business.

628
00:33:14,525 --> 00:33:18,629
So I worked for the people I trusted
and for the company.

629
00:33:20,465 --> 00:33:22,934
But as time passed,

630
00:33:24,302 --> 00:33:28,172
I realized
the world I believed in wasn't that clean.

631
00:33:29,907 --> 00:33:32,276
It was a place where unreasonable
things were allowed to happen.

632
00:33:35,146 --> 00:33:36,981
I knew that deep down,
but I had shut my eyes to it.

633
00:33:41,719 --> 00:33:43,688
Wakuda, what do you work for?

634
00:33:49,427 --> 00:33:50,728
I don't know.

635
00:33:53,464 --> 00:33:54,699
I want to work…

636
00:33:58,770 --> 00:34:01,839
for something I can truly believe in.

637
00:34:04,876 --> 00:34:05,777
But now…

638
00:34:10,515 --> 00:34:13,484
Something I can truly believe in…

639
00:34:15,987 --> 00:34:16,821
Yes.

640
00:34:19,123 --> 00:34:20,091
Kai is once again

641
00:34:20,925 --> 00:34:24,829
devoting himself
to something he believes in.

642
00:34:27,065 --> 00:34:28,900
That's why I want to support him.

643
00:34:34,105 --> 00:34:35,072
TOHTO CHUO BUSSAN SUCCEEDED IN M&amp;A
A NEW STEP TOWARDS BUSINESS EXPANSION

644
00:34:45,850 --> 00:34:46,684
Do we have sound?

645
00:34:46,751 --> 00:34:48,352
We do.

646
00:34:48,419 --> 00:34:50,254
DAINICHI TV STUDIO

647
00:34:51,889 --> 00:34:53,057
Ready.

648
00:34:54,592 --> 00:34:55,927
Start.

649
00:34:57,795 --> 00:34:59,030
WATER STATION

650
00:35:01,866 --> 00:35:04,769
I'm starving. What do you want for lunch?

651
00:35:04,836 --> 00:35:06,704
A fried chicken lunch box.

652
00:35:10,541 --> 00:35:12,176
How is it?

653
00:35:13,478 --> 00:35:15,079
No. I can't hear them at all.

654
00:35:15,146 --> 00:35:16,347
No good?

655
00:35:16,414 --> 00:35:17,949
This is hard.

656
00:35:18,015 --> 00:35:20,384
Hashiguchi, let's change the mic position.

657
00:35:20,451 --> 00:35:21,486
Okay.

658
00:35:22,153 --> 00:35:23,955
Okay.

659
00:35:25,256 --> 00:35:27,158
-Good work.
-Good work.

660
00:35:30,962 --> 00:35:33,865
THE NEW DESIGN-MIYAMOTO

661
00:35:39,103 --> 00:35:41,038
-Huh?
-The art staff sent over the set proposal.

662
00:35:41,105 --> 00:35:42,006
Oh.

663
00:35:42,073 --> 00:35:45,543
HAKONE EKIDEN

664
00:35:49,947 --> 00:35:51,082
Where's Miyamoto?

665
00:35:51,149 --> 00:35:51,983
In the studio.

666
00:35:52,550 --> 00:35:54,118
She's testing the water station.

667
00:35:54,652 --> 00:35:55,486
The water station?

668
00:35:56,053 --> 00:35:57,622
Toyama wants to broadcast

669
00:35:57,688 --> 00:35:59,957
the runners' water station exchanges
live during the race.

670
00:36:00,024 --> 00:36:02,660
She's testing whether the shotgun mic used

671
00:36:03,194 --> 00:36:05,730
for cup sounds in golf coverage

672
00:36:05,796 --> 00:36:06,831
might work.

673
00:36:06,898 --> 00:36:08,833
I see.

674
00:36:10,601 --> 00:36:11,469
Okay.

675
00:36:14,605 --> 00:36:16,774
THE OTHER HAKONE EKIDEN
INTERVIEW MATERIAL

676
00:36:18,643 --> 00:36:22,046
I think it was 2005.

677
00:36:23,381 --> 00:36:24,215
Found it.

678
00:36:24,282 --> 00:36:25,550
LEG TWO WINNER INTERVIEW
MASATO KAI

679
00:36:26,217 --> 00:36:27,885
Congrats
on the fastest time on the second leg.

680
00:36:27,952 --> 00:36:30,254
-Thank you.
-That was an incredible run.

681
00:36:32,089 --> 00:36:34,358
How did you feel when you
crossed the goal first?

682
00:36:34,425 --> 00:36:35,393
It's "finish."

683
00:36:36,794 --> 00:36:39,063
In track and field,
we say "finish," not "goal."

684
00:36:43,568 --> 00:36:45,469
I'm sorry.

685
00:36:49,140 --> 00:36:51,576
You were asking how I felt
when I finished first, right?

686
00:36:51,642 --> 00:36:52,510
Yes.

687
00:36:55,046 --> 00:36:56,714
DAINICHI TV

688
00:36:56,781 --> 00:36:59,617
I guess I was glad I'd believed in them.

689
00:37:04,088 --> 00:37:05,990
Coach Moroya taught me that.

690
00:37:06,057 --> 00:37:08,859
Trusting your teammates
is what matters most.

691
00:37:10,695 --> 00:37:12,196
That's why I was able to run.

692
00:37:14,031 --> 00:37:15,633
That's it.

693
00:37:16,167 --> 00:37:17,168
No.

694
00:37:17,235 --> 00:37:19,570
That's not what I mean!

695
00:37:19,637 --> 00:37:22,773
Forget it! I'm going over there!

696
00:37:24,108 --> 00:37:25,109
-I'll go too.
-Yeah.

697
00:37:25,176 --> 00:37:26,177
What's going on?

698
00:37:26,244 --> 00:37:27,979
They're testing the water station.

699
00:37:28,045 --> 00:37:30,047
They're getting nowhere!

700
00:37:33,317 --> 00:37:34,585
I'm going too.

701
00:37:37,655 --> 00:37:40,925
What about our meeting?

702
00:37:57,475 --> 00:37:58,809
Is everyone here?

703
00:37:59,977 --> 00:38:01,379
Except Kota.

704
00:38:03,981 --> 00:38:04,915
Hayato.

705
00:38:05,483 --> 00:38:07,652
Don't forget the most important thing.

706
00:38:08,219 --> 00:38:11,055
Our goal of finishing in the top three?

707
00:38:13,324 --> 00:38:14,292
Then…

708
00:38:16,594 --> 00:38:17,561
Trust.

709
00:38:19,196 --> 00:38:20,531
Trust your teammates.

710
00:38:24,835 --> 00:38:26,804
Coach Moroya taught me

711
00:38:27,605 --> 00:38:29,707
that's what matters most.

712
00:38:33,778 --> 00:38:35,479
There's something I want to tell everyone.

713
00:38:44,055 --> 00:38:45,690
It's about Kota.

714
00:38:47,758 --> 00:38:49,427
I still haven't heard from him.

715
00:38:51,529 --> 00:38:55,232
Honestly, I don't know what will happen.

716
00:38:57,702 --> 00:38:58,536
But

717
00:39:00,204 --> 00:39:01,572
I believe in him.

718
00:39:03,841 --> 00:39:07,678
I believe in Kota
and everyone who's here now.

719
00:39:08,546 --> 00:39:09,914
I want us to pass the sash together.

720
00:39:11,949 --> 00:39:13,784
That's what I believe now more than ever.

721
00:39:17,088 --> 00:39:18,022
Then

722
00:39:19,690 --> 00:39:21,125
how are we

723
00:39:22,626 --> 00:39:24,228
supposed to run

724
00:39:25,696 --> 00:39:27,732
as one team?

725
00:39:30,067 --> 00:39:32,236
There's backlash online.

726
00:39:32,303 --> 00:39:35,272
And we all have different
feelings about things.

727
00:39:36,507 --> 00:39:39,009
But we came together

728
00:39:40,177 --> 00:39:44,248
because we want to run.

729
00:39:48,953 --> 00:39:49,954
So

730
00:39:51,222 --> 00:39:53,958
let's do what we can now

731
00:39:55,459 --> 00:39:57,661
and be ready when Kota comes back.

732
00:39:59,730 --> 00:40:00,765
-Yes.
-Yes.

733
00:40:02,133 --> 00:40:03,100
Let's go.

734
00:40:03,768 --> 00:40:05,870
-Yes.
-Yes.

735
00:40:19,984 --> 00:40:22,420
What do you want with the drinks?

736
00:40:22,486 --> 00:40:25,589
Gyoza and assorted yakitori.

737
00:40:29,894 --> 00:40:33,497
Natsuki, how is it?

738
00:40:34,765 --> 00:40:36,534
No. I can barely hear it.

739
00:40:36,600 --> 00:40:38,936
WATER STATION ATTENDANT

740
00:40:39,003 --> 00:40:40,704
Hashiguchi, let's try running with them.

741
00:40:40,771 --> 00:40:41,839
Okay.

742
00:40:42,406 --> 00:40:45,576
How many tries is this?
I'm almost at my limit.

743
00:40:46,143 --> 00:40:47,511
Mr. Matsuzawa,

744
00:40:48,179 --> 00:40:50,648
give us something moving this time.

745
00:40:50,714 --> 00:40:52,483
Huh? What do you mean?

746
00:40:53,050 --> 00:40:57,221
I need some emotional energy or I'm done.

747
00:40:57,288 --> 00:40:59,757
Don't put that pressure on me.

748
00:41:00,324 --> 00:41:01,358
Okay, here we go.

749
00:41:04,195 --> 00:41:05,729
-Mr. Tokushige.
-How is it?

750
00:41:06,397 --> 00:41:08,365
It's difficult.

751
00:41:09,333 --> 00:41:11,936
Of course it won't work
from way over there!

752
00:41:12,436 --> 00:41:14,705
-Switch with him.
-Okay.

753
00:41:14,772 --> 00:41:16,407
I will.

754
00:41:16,474 --> 00:41:17,441
Thanks.

755
00:41:18,676 --> 00:41:21,612
Directionality is everything
with this shotgun mic.

756
00:41:21,679 --> 00:41:24,648
In this setup,
you need to aim it vertically.

757
00:41:25,249 --> 00:41:27,051
Okay, go ahead!

758
00:41:27,117 --> 00:41:29,887
Okay, Miyamoto! Try it!

759
00:41:31,689 --> 00:41:33,624
All right, here we go.

760
00:41:34,892 --> 00:41:35,893
Ready.

761
00:41:39,263 --> 00:41:40,264
Start!

762
00:41:41,031 --> 00:41:43,634
WATER STATION

763
00:41:52,710 --> 00:41:53,777
No good?

764
00:41:54,578 --> 00:41:55,813
Toyama!

765
00:41:56,981 --> 00:41:58,716
We're all fighting together!

766
00:41:59,750 --> 00:42:00,651
Huh?

767
00:42:01,452 --> 00:42:05,556
So you're not alone!

768
00:42:08,092 --> 00:42:10,461
We got it! We recorded it!

769
00:42:10,528 --> 00:42:12,296
You did it!

770
00:42:14,231 --> 00:42:15,299
How was it?

771
00:42:15,366 --> 00:42:18,969
Toyama! We're all fighting together!

772
00:42:22,840 --> 00:42:24,508
So you're not alone!

773
00:42:25,910 --> 00:42:28,245
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

774
00:42:28,312 --> 00:42:30,180
-Thank you!
-Oh!

775
00:42:30,247 --> 00:42:31,815
Natsuki!

776
00:42:31,882 --> 00:42:34,418
Never give up!

777
00:42:35,286 --> 00:42:37,922
Matsuzawa, that was pretty good.
It actually moved me.

778
00:42:39,490 --> 00:42:43,060
Actually, Mr. Tokushige said that to me
a long time ago.

779
00:42:43,127 --> 00:42:44,328
Really?

780
00:42:44,395 --> 00:42:47,565
He probably doesn't even remember.

781
00:42:48,165 --> 00:42:50,167
That actually got to me too.

782
00:42:50,234 --> 00:42:51,135
Huh?

783
00:42:53,704 --> 00:42:54,939
Never…

784
00:42:55,005 --> 00:42:56,707
He can say some good things.

785
00:42:57,975 --> 00:43:00,644
HAKONE EKIDEN

786
00:43:04,848 --> 00:43:05,849
Thank you.

787
00:43:07,952 --> 00:43:12,222
I assumed it was normal that
we couldn't pick up the runners' voices.

788
00:43:12,990 --> 00:43:14,925
I never even thought about trying.

789
00:43:16,994 --> 00:43:18,195
Somewhere along the way,

790
00:43:18,262 --> 00:43:20,598
I guess I got used to it.

791
00:43:22,399 --> 00:43:24,201
Toyama and the others

792
00:43:24,268 --> 00:43:25,869
reminded me to go back to basics.

793
00:43:27,972 --> 00:43:30,207
-Me too.
-Huh?

794
00:43:30,774 --> 00:43:32,109
That's right.

795
00:43:33,477 --> 00:43:35,946
If you have something
you believe in, that's enough.

796
00:43:39,817 --> 00:43:41,986
Let's go with the first design.

797
00:43:43,220 --> 00:43:44,154
Okay.

798
